description: Keep every HELM website release simple, audience-focused, and publicly presentable
alwaysApply: true
---

# Public audience release guard

- HELM is a simple framework with practical guides. Every public page must help
  its intended reader understand something or take a useful next step.
- Never publish unfinished, review-oriented, maintainer-only, or
  audience-inappropriate material.
- Keep technical implementation, release mechanics, internal evidence labels,
  correction registers, task IDs, source-review logs, and acceptance criteria
  out of website copy, navigation, metadata, feeds, and downloads.
- Use plain language, short explanations, concrete examples, and descriptive
  links. Explain specialist terms only when the intended audience needs them.
- Preserve honest limitations in reader-friendly language; do not make
  unsupported guidance sound proven.
- Every public route must declare its audience and purpose in
  `scripts/public-audiences.json`.
- Follow `docs/public-publishing.md` and update the reader-facing Updates entry
  for public changes.
- Review rendered desktop, mobile, no-JavaScript, metadata, and feed output.
- Run `npm run check`. Never weaken, bypass, or add exceptions to
  `scripts/public-content-guard.mjs` to make a release pass.
- If any public surface is not ready to send directly to its intended reader,
  simplify it or keep it out of the release.
